        // attacker calls withdrawAll: attacker has credit attackerDeposit and will get paid; during its receive it will try to re-enter and call withdrawAll again,
        // which will attempt to withdraw victim's funds only if the contract's logic or ordering allows it. This exercises reentrancy on the mutant.
        c.withdrawAll();

        // Now assert the general property about c's balance after a withdraw: for the reference contract, after any withdrawAll completes,
        // the contract balance must equal expectedAfter. For the mutant, reentrancy can cause more Ether to be drained leaving balance < expectedAfter.
        assertTrue(address(c).balance == expectedAfter);
